41 - - **The §11.3 serving half** (F54) — `serve_entry(entry, req_headers, now_secs)` (`http.rs`): the ONE call a host makes to serve a stored entry — the canonical conditional comparison (`conditional_response`: weak `If-None-Match` lists and `*`, then `If-Modified-Since` against the entry's `Last-Modified`) and the §11.3 header set (`cache_control` from the policy, the entry's ETag, the `Date`) composed into one `ServeOutcome` (`NotModified` carries the validator set a 304 SHOULD have — RFC 9110 §15.4.5; `Full` carries the stored headers verbatim with the generated set filling only the gaps, one header per name). The helpers the audit named zero-consumer works compose here at last, and the serving decision gains the capability the hand-rolled matches never had: an `If-Modified-Since`-only re-check against an unchanged `Last-Modified` answers 304 instead of re-downloading. `crates/cache/examples/conditional.rs` serves one entry three ways (first visit, ETag re-check, IMS-only re-check)
